  "source_note": "Melody transcribed from the complete Ebersberger/Jurtenland LilyPond melody (D major), transposed down a whole tone to C. Historical authorship corroborated by Kinder wollen singen. All 16 bars included. The F# in the middle section and sixteenth-note bell motif are retained; this is not an all-diatonic beginner tune.",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "practice_notes_de": [
    "Erst die vier Takte des Glockenrufs langsam spielen.",
    "Die vier Sechzehntel als gleichmäßige kurze Gruppe üben.",
    "Im Mittelteil Fis gesondert suchen; erst danach die Bassbegleitung ergänzen."
  ],
  "harmony_note": "Functional chord stream transcribed from the linked LilyPond/ABC source. It is not yet a mechanically playable bass part: reduce or omit unsupported triads and direction conflicts for the 8-bass Corso.",
  "rights_status": "Traditional/public-domain melody; new machine-readable transcription; no lyrics or recorded audio copied.",
  "rights_note": "Jurtenland/Ebersberger source explicitly labels melody and lyrics as public domain and its notation freely copyable. Kinder wollen singen supplies historical composer/source information and publishes its new notation as CC0. Only the traditional melody and simple harmonic functions are represented here; no modern rendered edition is redistributed."
